{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016eQnqRvChDeKff7duDUVXB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-folder, stdlib-only personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that has grown a substantial R&D \"mission control\" layer on top of a markdown task manager. Grounded claims:\n\n- **What it is at the core:** A self-contained Python (stdlib-only) productivity app where plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) are the source of truth â€” no database, no external dependencies. It lives entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor`.\n\n- **What it ships (the deliverable):** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a standalone HTTP server that generates the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes back to markdown directly. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) exposes the same logic and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core task management:** Tasks move through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored) across domain files, with priority/energy/due/notes fields, an inbox capture, per-domain views, and daily activity logs.\n\n- **R&D control surface (the big add-on):** Each project gets a window that acts as a cockpit for \"trio\" work â€” the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** skill pipeline (Research Â· Planning Â· Build lanes). This has been built across three generations:\n  - **v2:** session model, cached/validated summaries, a Grass Catchers idea lane, deliverable declare/pin, and an interactive stream-json REPL terminal.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\":** real **ConPTY terminals** (via the lone declared native exception `pywinpty`, lazily imported in `pty_manager.py` only), per-session **git-worktree isolation**, a durable session registry, a stacking window manager with xterm.js, in-place expandable summaries, stage handoffs, a runnable deliverable preview (hard-guarded to never bind 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding. Built and merged to master 2026-06-12.\n  - **v4 (in progress, current branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v4`):** redesign toward a calm single-screen cockpit where each lane tile shows one honest status light and expands in place to stack a summary over a real resizable terminal; the v3 ConPTY path is locked as the one terminal substrate, with the skill auto-loading/greeting exactly once per new session.\n\n- **Self-verification:** A daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway test server, exercises every endpoint and task state, and walks the v2 and v3 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, no real ConPTY, isolated temp dirs) â€” writing dated reports and surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\nOne caveat on the \"what it does\" framing: the v4 cockpit described in the locked North Star is still being built on this branch, so that single-screen experience is design-frozen and in-flight, not yet shipped to master."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":41003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24056d51-a898-4464-b89d-b312ea957a67","uuid":"c50f1972-371f-4dc1-bba1-162a1b2c0ce4","request_id":"req_011CbykjKVsPJbKw1dXcZSus"}
